  "final_answer": "All three deliverables are written and verified in `/app`:\n\n- **`fairhousing_audit.csv`** \u2014 header `section_id,finding`, one row per section SEC-01\u2026SEC-30 in inventory order, exactly two columns (no extras). Findings joined with `|` in the order `PROHIBITED_PERSONAL_NARRATIVE|PROTECTED_CLASS_LANGUAGE|DISCLAIMER_MISSING`.\n- **`fairhousing_memo.md`** \u2014 per-section reasoning table plus the key interpretive points legal needs to sign off without re-reading RE-FH-9.\n- **`results.json`** \u2014 `{\"section_count\":30,\"flagged_count\":22,\"personal_narrative_count\":7,\"protected_lang_count\":14,\"disclaimer_missing_count\":11}`.\n\nKey judgement calls, all driven by the standard as amended (not the book's text):\n- Audited against the 11-class list (\u00a75a added **marital status** and **source of income**); every legacy notice is abridged on those two, which both fails \u00a74 for responsible roles and strips the \u00a73 exemption so the notice's own terms trip \u00a72.\n- \u00a74 responsible roles = `closing_page` + `agent_bio` (\u00a75b). `disclosure_block` is **not** responsible, so its abridged SEC-04/SEC-22 get `PROTECTED_CLASS_LANGUAGE` but not `DISCLAIMER_MISSING` \u2014 flagged as a gap in the memo.\n- \u00a71 is role-independent (7 hits); \u00a73 only shelters notice text, never surrounding prose (why SEC-19 still trips \u00a72 despite a complete notice); \u00a73 exempts from \u00a72 only (why SEC-08/24/29 still trip \u00a71 despite a complete notice). SEC-07 is the lone section tripping all three.",
